<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Momotombo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Momotombo is a conical stratovolcano rising to about 1,300 metres on the northern shore of Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/managua">Managua</a> in western Nicaragua. Earthquakes and eruptions in the early seventeenth century led to the abandonment of the first colonial city of León, at its foot, in 1610. In 1902 opponents of a Nicaraguan canal sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> senators Nicaraguan stamps showing Momotombo smoking, helping to persuade them to choose the Panama route.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/momotombo.jpg" alt="Momotombo" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Momotombo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
